---
// The first screen, as ruled on 2026-11-20 (docs/design/2026-11-20-tracker-design-proposal.md,
// section 7): the line above the title, the question as the title, the ranking in its three
// groups, then on the right the headline card, the paragraph for a newcomer, the last-checked
// line, the two buttons and the latest news. On a phone the headline card moves up between the
// title and the ranking. Every number comes from the records (src/lib/tracker.ts).
// The copy is draft (design proposal section 8): not yet through the voice checks.
//
// Until 2026-11-21 this page was the project's log front page ("3 of 8 stages delivered"); that
// content now lives on /tests/ and the pages under it.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Ranking from '../components/Ranking.astro';
import HeadCard from '../components/HeadCard.astro';
import LatestNews from '../components/LatestNews.astro';
import N from '../components/N.astro';
import { tk, word } from '../lib/tracker';
---

<Base title="Minimum Viable Mind: how the theories of consciousness are holding up" strict>
  <section class="home-top">
    <div>
      <p class="above"><b>What is the least a mind needs?</b> Every theory of consciousness gives an answer. Here is how <N v={tk.listed_count} t={word(tk.listed_count)} /> of them are holding up.</p>
      <h1 class="tquestion">How far has the science of consciousness got in testing its theories?</h1>
      <div class="m-only"><HeadCard /></div>
      <Ranking />
    </div>
    <aside>
      <div class="d-only"><HeadCard /></div>
      <div class="aside-new">
        <p class="newcomer">Each theory is scored three ways, by rules written down before any theory was scored: how well published studies back it, how clearly it can be tested (whether it is stated so that a study could prove it wrong), and how much of it is still untested. One of the theories is this site's own, the account argued on <a href="https://sentient-horizons.com/positions/">Sentient Horizons</a>; it is scored by the same rules, and an outside reader makes the first judgement on every one of its rows.</p>
        <p class="strip">
          {tk.headline.last_reading
            ? <>Last checked <N v={tk.headline.last_reading} />. <a href="/about/#reading">See the week's reading</a>.</>
            : <>No weekly reading yet: the predictions have not yet been read against new papers. The scores were last worked out on <N v={tk.headline.worked_out_on} t={tk.headline.worked_out_on_long} />. <a href="/about/#reading">About the weekly reading</a>.</>}
        </p>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a class="btn" href="/about/#why">How the tests came out</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/about/#who">Who is asking</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <LatestNews />
    </aside>
  </section>
</Base>
